.TH MD_CONFIG_INIT 3 "2026-10-16" "libmorsedec 0.3.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
md_config_init \- initialize decoder configuration defaults
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <morsedec.h>

void md_config_init(struct morsedec_config *config);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Initialize decoder configuration defaults.
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I config
Configuration structure to initialize. NULL is accepted and has no effect.
.SH RETURN VALUE
This function returns no value.
.SH REMARKS
Writes audio defaults: sample_rate=48000, fft_size=0, hop_size=0,
min_frequency=200, max_frequency=1200, max_channels=32, initial_wpm=0. Zero
FFT and hop sizes request automatic geometry. Call this before changing
selected fields; a wholly zero-initialized configuration is invalid. For an
explicit I/Q configuration set signed band edges before calling md_new_iq();
initialization itself always uses audio defaults.
.SH THREAD SAFETY
Independent configuration objects can be initialized concurrently. Serialize
access to the same object.
.SH VERSION
This md_ entry point is available since libmorsedec 0.2.0.
Version 0.3.0 uses the float API and shared-library ABI 2.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmorsedec (3),
.BR md_new (3),
.BR md_new_iq (3)
